From: Yocto Swift layer
Subject: [PATCH] Include stdint.h for uintptr_t in bundled GoogleTest

The bundled GoogleTest death-test implementation uses uintptr_t but does
not include the header that defines it. Newer Clang/libc combinations do
not expose it transitively, causing llbuild's test support to fail to
compile even when the tests themselves are not run.

--- a/utils/unittest/googletest/src/gtest-death-test.cc
+++ b/utils/unittest/googletest/src/gtest-death-test.cc
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@
 // This file implements death tests.
 
 #include "gtest/gtest-death-test.h"
 
+#include <stdint.h>
 #include <utility>
 
 #include "gtest/internal/gtest-port.h"
